## Generic Types and Generic Arrays

Generic functions can define both generic types with generic axis lengths as demonstrated in this example where the `toFloats` now takes an input array of any shape as long as its data type satisfies the `ints` constraint.

```code:main
package main

type ints interface {
    int32 | int64
}

type floats interface {
    float32 | float64
}

func toFloats[Dest floats, Src ints, Shape []intlen](a Src) Dest {
    return Dest(a)
}

func Main() (float32, float64) {
    a := [2][3]int64{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}} 
    f32a := toFloats[float32, int64](a)
    // In the following call, the compiler uses type inference
    // to determine the type of the function parameter Src from its argument.
    f64a := toFloats[float64](a)
    return f32a, f64a
}
```

